        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-14T15:48:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should any new host operations get blocked during the 7 second online delay?  Should this routine check the current port state?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb4e31a3_c5d861a9",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 322,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-15T01:36:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel It\u0027s not necessary to block host operation during this 7 seconds online delay.\nThis is based on host(FWUPD) is following fixed steps. \nAfter firmware update, host should wait 5 seconds (for retimer to come to functional state). \nThen host requests PD port 0 online: a) disconnect USB mux; b) resume port.\nSince 5 seconds is not enforced, this CL will handle this case.\n\nHere is my reasoning:\n1. If retimer is accessible, both a) \u0026 b) are succeed, then port status is RETIMER_ONLINE; By the time retimer_check_online() is triggered, it will not do anything to this port since it is not RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED.\nMeanwhile, during this 7 seconds delay, the port can do offline again; it can even request online again, but port is not suspended, it will get error back as expected.\n\n2. If retimer is not accessible; At online request step a), port state is changed to RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED, host fails to set USB mux to 0; and host won\u0027t do b) to resume port. After 7 seconds, retimer_check_online() will resume this port.\nFWUPD will not do anything with this port after this failure.\nUnless someone manually does offline upon failure, this will change port state. I assume only developer could do so.\n@Kranthi, correct me if I miss any scenario in host/FWUPD side.",
      "parentUuid": "35c01629_0daac609",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d175dbd_89010bba",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 322,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T16:38:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding #2 - you say if UPDATE_DISCONNECT fails, the AP won\u0027t send UPDATE_RESUME_PD.  However, this CL is getting added because the AP does something unexpected (fails to wait 5 seconds before online request).\n\nIf the EC sets the state to RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED, but the AP still sends UPDATE_RESUME_PD, the state will get changed to RETIMER_ONLINE without successfully completing the `usb_mux_set(USB_NONE)`.\n\nThe UPDATE_SUSPEND_PD command also has the potential to change the state from RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED before the a call to `usb_mux_set(USB_NONE)` by the deferred task.\n\nThe RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED deferred call is guaranteed to change the state back to RETIMER_ONLINE, even if the deferred `usb_mux_set()` fails.  \n\nI think blocking all host operations while the state is RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED is a safer approach.\n\nI would like someone from the host side to comment on this as well.",
      "parentUuid": "eb4e31a3_c5d861a9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cbe8f87_db719f86",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 322,
      "author": {
        "id": 1181774
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T17:40:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think blocking all host operations while the state is RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED is a safer approach.\n\nI\u0027ve not being following the CL discussion, but this approach seems the most logical. We should not pre-suppose any specific behavior from the host side. \n\nWhat is the situation where the AP would send `UPDATE_RESUME_PD` after `RETIMER_ONLINE_REQUESTED` has been scheduled?\n\nAny such request which can result in a race should be blocked and an error message should be surfaced to the AP. The AP should deal with the errors.\n\n\u003e Since 5 seconds is not enforced, this CL will handle this case.\n\nIf during an \"port online\" request the right error (-EBUSY) were surfaced to the `AP` and specifically `fwupd`, then I don\u0027t see why it wouldn\u0027t handle it gracefully (retry etc). FWICT right now it just gets an EIO error and so it doesn\u0027t proceed any further. campello@ or Kranthi might know more about this.",
      "parentUuid": "8d175dbd_89010bba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27fd875f_915ee3b0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 322,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T21:37:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we need comments from host side/FWUPD.\n\nMy understanding is the ONLINE request from host is 2-step action; 1st: requests EC disconnect USB mux; 2nd: requests EC to resume. host won\u0027t send out resume request separately. So if \"disconnect USB mux\" is failed, no more request from host/FWUPD.",
      "parentUuid": "9cbe8f87_db719f86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5a26f51_e21ae6a0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 322,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T22:05:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes thats right currently issuing online request ( no 5 sec wait) results in un recoverable -EIO system error , this is where Daniel was more concerned about.",
      "parentUuid": "9cbe8f87_db719f86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2d68e300_6bb8fff6",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 322,
      "author": {
        "id": 1181774
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T22:11:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So if \"disconnect USB mux\" is failed, no more request from host/FWUPD.\n\nWhat about AP resets? Are there chip hooks which try to resume PD on a port if it was earlier suspended (I think there are, but I may be misremembering).\n\nRegardless, any request that comes in while the timeout has not elapsed should just return -EBUSY to the kernel. That solves the issue of raciness, and also lets fwupd actually recover and retry (with EIO is just gives up).",
      "parentUuid": "a5a26f51_e21ae6a0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
