      "writtenOn": "2022-06-24T16:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this has been discussed many times and I have expressed the reasoning why on the Buganizer bug b/212235056#comment76. Please continue this conversation on the bug if needed. \n\nIn general, I think expecting a sysfs interface to be used appropriately by user space (fwupd, or any other client with -possibly concurrently- access to the interface) and failing unrecoverable otherwise is a bad idea.",
      "parentUuid": "a19b26ef_f4493294",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 322,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 322,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "ee4bc1aa1b42338e429cd230c080b738483559c1",
